@meta
id: 22-05
title: Started at the wrong end
chapter: 22
type: lesson
skills: visual-char, visual-line
par: 25
minutes: 4
vscode: click, Shift-click, realise you missed the heading, start again
open: payments.md

@brief
A selection has two ends: the anchor where you pressed `v`, and the
cursor, which is the only end you can move. Half the time you discover,
with the region highlighted, that it needs to grow at the *other* end.
Dropping the selection and starting again is what a mouse user does.

`o` swaps the ends. The cursor jumps to the anchor, the anchor stays
where the cursor was, and the selection is untouched. Now the other end
is the one that moves.

The "Old checkout path" section of the payments doc is out of date.
Remove the whole section: its heading, its paragraph, and one of the
two blank lines around it, so that "Refunds" runs straight into
"Retries" with a single blank line between them.

@keys
| `o` | swap the cursor to the other end of the selection |
| `ip` | select the paragraph |
| `k` | extend the selection upward |

@hints
Search for a word that is only in the section's paragraph — `gateway`
will do — and select the paragraph with `vip`. The heading is above it,
and the cursor is at the bottom.
--
`o` moves the cursor to the top of the selection. Now `k` extends it
upward: the blank line, the heading, the blank line above the heading.
--
`/gateway` `Enter`, `vip`, `o`, `kkk`, `d`.

@solution
    /gateway<Enter> v i p o k k k d :wq<Enter>

Twenty-one keystrokes. Without `o` you would have had to `Esc`, move up
three lines, and reselect downward — more keys, and a good chance of
landing a line off. With `o` the region you already had is kept and
simply grows at the end that needed it.

`o` works in all three visual modes. In block mode there is also `O`,
which swaps to the other corner on the same line, for when a column
selection needs to grow to the left instead of the right.

@start payments.md
# Payments

## Refunds

Refunds go through the payment service and are capped at the order
total. Partial refunds are allowed.

## Old checkout path

The legacy gateway is still called for orders placed before the
migration. It is read only and will be removed once the last of
those orders is closed.

## Retries

Failed captures are retried three times with a backoff of ten
seconds, then the order is flagged for manual review.

@expected payments.md
# Payments

## Refunds

Refunds go through the payment service and are capped at the order
total. Partial refunds are allowed.

## Retries

Failed captures are retried three times with a backoff of ten
seconds, then the order is flagged for manual review.
